A||||5||WisconsinGT||Update on EGR/Spacer||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||04-16-2000||01:11 PM||||Well, I disassembled the EGR area. I found out that the spacer was warped. So I removed it. I am glad that the EGR Tube is flexible. I am noticing that my idle is a bit higher. From dead on 800 to a slight fluctuation between 900-1000. I do not know if it is a problem or not yet. I do hate the semi-plastic (Very brittle) Vac. tubes that run all over the damn engine.  Anyway, here is the link to the pictures of the spacer. <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=608824&a=4665187." TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=608824&a=4665187.</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ed||04-16-2000||04:28 PM||||Let us know if you think the idle is not right.  We've got the tune-up specs.  It sounds okay based on your description.  A variance of about 75 rpm is said to be okay in the V-6.   <P>The idle varies with the transmission, drive or neutral, and whether you've bypassed the computer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||04-16-2000||05:10 PM||||If the above link does not work, try the following two links.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=608824&a=4443093&p=19632165" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=608824&a=4443093&p=19632165</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=608824&a=4443093&p=19632168" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=608824&a=4443093&p=19632168</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-16-2000||09:26 PM||||Idle can be rock solid or bounce around some on both the V6 and 4. Depends on the specific conditions at the time. May not be a problem as long as it stays under 1000rpm.<P>Hard Vacuum line can be replaced. It's available in most parts stores. You heat it in hot water to form it. Most times you can reuse the rubber connectors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||04-17-2000||01:15 PM||||Thanks Ogre-Ed! Hey Ogre, do I have to use a hard vacuum line? Could I run rubber vac. hose around the engine? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-17-2000||09:04 PM||||I replaced all the hard vacuum lines that run under the plenum with regular rubber ones. To keep the rubber ones straight and away from hot/delicate areas I bought a handful of the small spark plug wire looms. They are usually on the rack that has the red "HELP" sign. These are the racks that usually have the odd parts you usually don't need but when you do are hard to find. Like little clips and door handle pieces.||||reg||1
